// Bollinger Band Reversion
//
// John Bollinger's bands: a moving average with rails at two standard deviations. Traded
// as reversion — buy the lower rail, leave at the middle.
//
// Bollinger himself warned against exactly this reading: a touch of the lower band in a
// downtrend is not a bargain, it is a downtrend. It is here because it is the most common
// published use, and because seeing it fail out of sample teaches more than being told.
strategy("Bollinger Reversion", overlay = true)

[upper, mid, lower] = bb(close, 20, 2)

plot(upper, title = "Upper",  color = color.mute)
plot(mid,   title = "Middle", color = color.accent)
plot(lower, title = "Lower",  color = color.mute)

if crossunder(close, lower)
    strategy.entry("reversion", strategy.long)

if crossover(close, mid)
    strategy.close("reversion")
